  <block id="p4" kind="prose">
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="11" spacingafter="6" background="#FFF8E9">Shared pile size, spacing and cap dimensions are read from Bridge Geometry (235-in cap). Use nominal pile width only, without a placement envelope. Wall positions are the wall lines of the CAD model of 19 October 2026; the 8-in cheek webs outside the cap ends are not part of this screen. In that model the side walls stand 114 in from the pile row, at the 24-in criterion within 0.0002 in: the side-wall rows below read MEETS CLEAR or SHORTFALL only by the last digits of the model coordinates.</paragraph>
  </block>
  <block id="p5" kind="prose">
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Nominal square pile width.</paragraph>
  </block>
  <block id="p6" kind="prose">
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Pile spacing along the row.</paragraph>
  </block>
  <block id="p7" kind="prose">
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Trial front-wall strap width; use vendor dimension.</paragraph>
  </block>
  <block id="p8" kind="prose">
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Additional strap-edge gap; zero is tangency.</paragraph>
  </block>
  <block id="p9" kind="prose">
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Selected front-wall plan skew, to either side of the wall normal.</paragraph>
  </block>
  <block id="p10" kind="prose">
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Specified side pile-face to back-of-facing minimum; no side strap check.</paragraph>
  </block>
  <block id="p11" kind="prose">
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Round the computed front setback upward by this increment.</paragraph>
  </block>
  <block id="p12" kind="prose">
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Nominal pile half-width; no placement allowance.</paragraph>
  </block>
  <block id="p13" kind="prose">
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Front wall: minimum clear from nominal pile face to back of facing.</paragraph>
  </block>
  <block id="p14" kind="prose">
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Front wall: adopted clear rounded UP.</paragraph>
  </block>
  <block id="p15" kind="prose">
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Pile center to front-wall limit.</paragraph>
  </block>
  <block id="p16" kind="prose">
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="5">Pile center to either side-wall limit.</paragraph>
  </block>
  <block id="p17" kind="prose">
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="6" background="#F1F5FA">DERIVATION: S sin alpha - h cos alpha = w/2 + c. Solve for S using h = nominal pile width / 2. The centered nominal geometry is symmetric for positive or negative skew. No pile placement term enters this expression.</paragraph>
  </block>
  <block id="p18" kind="prose">
    <paragraph fontfamily="Times New Roman" fontsize="10" spacingafter="6">Red open boundary shows computed front and specified side offsets. There is no rear-wall criterion. Gray is the cap; black is the current back of facing. Local x runs across the piles and +y into the approach.</paragraph>
  </block>
